---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import { heroPhotos } from '../data/photos';
---

<Layout title="About" description="Learn how Silent Meeting, Meeting for Worship, shared silence, and spoken messages unfold at 429 Friends.">
  <Hero compact eyebrow="About the gathering" title="Listening together, without an agenda." description="Meeting for Worship is the Quaker name for a Silent Meeting. We gather in a circle, become quiet together, and pay attention to what rises in the stillness." image={heroPhotos.about} imageAlt="A coral honeysuckle bloom in the garden at 429 Friends." />

  <Section eyebrow="Silent Meeting" title="There is no program to follow." intro="Meeting for Worship is often described in plain language as a Silent Meeting. No one leads the hour, delivers a sermon, or asks you to agree with a statement of belief. The shared practice is attention: becoming still enough to notice what is present.">
    <div class="card-grid card-grid--three">
      <Card title="Settling" icon="self_improvement"><p>At first, the silence may feel unfamiliar. There is nothing to achieve. Let your mind wander and return at its own pace.</p></Card>
      <Card title="Listening" icon="hearing"><p>Some people reflect, pray, notice the natural world, or simply rest. Each person finds their own way into the quiet.</p></Card>
      <Card title="Sharing" icon="record_voice_over"><p>If someone feels moved to speak, they may stand and offer a short message. Most of the hour remains quiet, with space between messages.</p></Card>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="soft" eyebrow="The shape of an hour" title="What the meeting feels like">
    <ol class="timeline">
      <li><span>01</span><div><h3>We gather</h3><p>Choose a place in the circle and get comfortable. A host welcomes newcomers before the meeting begins.</p></div></li>
      <li><span>02</span><div><h3>We become quiet</h3><p>The group settles naturally into silence. There is no signal that you need to watch for and no prescribed posture.</p></div></li>
      <li><span>03</span><div><h3>We listen</h3><p>The quiet continues for about 45–60 minutes. Spoken messages may arise, with space between them.</p></div></li>
      <li><span>04</span><div><h3>We reconnect</h3><p>The meeting closes with a simple greeting. Introductions and unhurried conversation follow.</p></div></li>
    </ol>
  </Section>

  <Section narrow>
    <Callout title="You do not have to call yourself a Quaker." icon="waving_hand">
      <p>People of many beliefs—and no particular belief—can find meaning in shared silence. Curiosity and respect are enough.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/first-time-here/">Read the first-time visitor guide<span class="material-symbols-rounded" aria-hidden="true">arrow_forward</span></a>
    </Callout>
  </Section>
</Layout>
